Bash(cd E:/Projects/POS && gh issue create --title "Square Menu Item Display with object-fit: contain" --label "new-feature,ux" --milestone "v1.0 - MVP" --body "$\(cat <<'EOF'
## Problem
Menu item images vary wildly in aspect ratio:
- Tall drinks: ~145x285 \(1:2 portrait\)
- Hot coffee: ~290x280 \(nearly square\)
- Noodles: ~485x405 \(landscape\)
- Street bites platter: 764x195 \(4:1 ultra-wide\)

All are RGBA PNGs with transparent/neutral backgrounds.

## Solution
Display all menu items in **perfect square containers** using:

```css
.menuItemImage {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  background-color: #FAF5EF; /* warm cream, matches theme */
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

.menuItemImage img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: contain;
  padding: 8px; /* breathing room inside square */
}
```

## Why `contain` over `cover`
- `cover` would crop tall drinks \(losing the glass top\) and wide platters \(losing edges\)
- `contain` shows the full item, padding fills naturally with the warm cream bg
- Consistent visual treatment across all categories

## Affected Components
- Kiosk MenuBrowse grid
- Kiosk ItemDetail hero image
- POS Solo Counter product photo
- Prep/Kitchen Station product photo
- Admin Menu Management item grid

## Depends on
- #16 \(menu item images update\)
EOF
\)")
